WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:20.584
the church clock struck two, Jean Valjean awoke in the bishop's house.

2
00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:28.311
Many thoughts passed through his mind, but one kept returning: there was a small fortune in silver in

3
00:00:28.331 --> 00:00:29.032
the next room!

4
00:00:30.184 --> 00:00:34.985
The six plates and the ladle were worth twice what he had earned for 19 years of prison

5
00:00:35.025 --> 00:00:40.387
labor. Valjean sat on the edge of the bed, thinking about the silver for an hour.

6
00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:43.928
He might have remained there longer if the clock hadn't struck again.

7
00:00:45.168 --> 00:00:47.369
The clock seemed to say, "Let's go!"

8
00:00:48.189 --> 00:00:51.950
So Valjean stood up and went to the door that led to the bishop's bedroom.

9
00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.050
The bishop had left it ajar.

10
00:00:55.411 --> 00:00:59.732
Valjean pushed the door lightly with his fingertip, and it opened a little wider.

11
00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:05.153
He waited a moment and then pushed the door again, more boldly this time.

12
00:01:06.294 --> 00:01:08.754
The door opened wide with a loud creak.

13
00:01:09.495 --> 00:01:11.355
Valjean froze with his heart pounding.

14
00:01:12.656 --> 00:01:14.076
But no one in the house woke up.

15
00:01:14.696 --> 00:01:21.398
Valjean peered into the room and saw the bishop sleeping peacefully, a beam of moonlight illuminating his pale

16
00:01:21.438 --> 00:01:25.119
face. Valjean slipped silently into the room.

17
00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:30.390
He opened the cupboard at the head of the bed and removed the basket containing the ladle and

18
00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:37.335
plates. Once outside he threw away the basket, ran across the garden, and leaped over the low, white

19
00:01:37.415 --> 00:01:43.819
wall. The next morning the bishop was walking in the garden when his housekeeper dashed out of the

20
00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:47.041
house. "The silver basket has disappeared!"

21
00:01:47.642 --> 00:01:48.722
cried Madame Magloire.

22
00:01:48.742 --> 00:01:51.304
"I just found it here in the garden."

23
00:01:51.624 --> 00:01:53.926
The bishop calmly handed the basket to her.

24
00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:56.428
"But there's nothing in it!

25
00:01:57.088 --> 00:01:59.910
That man who came last night must have stolen the silver."

26
00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:05.973
Madame Magloire ran back into the bishop's house while he bent sadly over a flower lying on the

27
00:02:06.013 --> 00:02:08.695
ground. The basket had broken its stem.

28
00:02:09.936 --> 00:02:12.657
Madame Magloire came running into the garden again.

29
00:02:12.677 --> 00:02:14.378
"He's gone!"

30
00:02:14.838 --> 00:02:15.879
she said to the bishop.

31
00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:18.420
The bishop was silent for a moment.

32
00:02:19.001 --> 00:02:23.523
Then he said, "I held on to that silver for a long time when I should have given

33
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:24.144
it to the poor.

34
00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:30.523
Our visitor was evidently a poor man, so it's appropriate that the silver now belongs to him."

35
00:02:30.543 --> 00:02:33.484
"But what are you going to eat from?

36
00:02:33.865 --> 00:02:39.748
We don't have any—" Their discussion was interrupted by the bishop's sister calling to them from a window.

37
00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:42.309
"Someone's knocking at the front door!"

38
00:02:42.669 --> 00:02:44.250
cried Mademoiselle Baptistine.

39
00:02:45.191 --> 00:02:49.433
Madame Magloire hurried into the house with the bishop following slowly behind her.

40
00:02:49.453 --> 00:02:50.894
"Come in!"

41
00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:53.175
said the bishop when he reached the front room.

42
00:02:54.055 --> 00:02:57.217
The door opened and there stood three policemen.

43
00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.258
One held Jean Valjean by his collar.

44
00:03:00.278 --> 00:03:05.840
"I'm so happy to see you again," the bishop said kindly to Valjean.

45
00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.381
"I meant for you to have my candlesticks too.

46
00:03:09.242 --> 00:03:11.663
Why didn't you take them along with your ladle and plates?

47
00:03:12.123 --> 00:03:14.984
They're also made of silver and will bring a good price."

48
00:03:16.024 --> 00:03:20.586
Valjean's eyes widened, and he looked at the bishop with a stunned expression.

49
00:03:20.606 --> 00:03:24.768
"He seemed to be running away from something," said one of the policemen.

50
00:03:25.236 --> 00:03:27.057
"So we stopped him and found your silver."

51
00:03:27.077 --> 00:03:31.038
"And then I'm sure he told you that he'd spent the night here and that I'd given it

52
00:03:31.078 --> 00:03:31.398
to him.

53
00:03:32.058 --> 00:03:34.639
I hope you can see that you've made a terrible mistake."

54
00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:39.101
"If that's the truth, then we'll let him go," said the same policeman.

55
00:03:39.121 --> 00:03:41.761
"Let him go," said the bishop.

56
00:03:42.142 --> 00:03:47.223
Then he went to the mantel, picked up the two candlesticks, and handed them to Valjean.

57
00:03:47.843 --> 00:03:49.504
"Here are your candlesticks, my friend."

58
00:03:50.908 --> 00:03:55.151
Madame Magloire and Mademoiselle Baptistine were too amazed to speak.

59
00:03:56.232 --> 00:03:59.474
Valjean took the candlesticks with a wild look in his eye.

60
00:03:59.494 --> 00:04:05.418
"By the way, my friend," continued the bishop, "the next time you visit, you don't have to come

61
00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:06.119
through the garden.

62
00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:10.582
You can always come in by the front door; it's never locked."

63
00:04:11.503 --> 00:04:15.465
The policemen left, and the bishop turned his attention to Valjean again.

64
00:04:16.346 --> 00:04:22.422
In a quiet voice he said, "Never forget that you've promised me to use this silver to become

65
00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.543
an honest man.

66
00:04:24.123 --> 00:04:25.604
Now go in peace."

67
00:04:26.785 --> 00:04:31.968
Valjean knew that he hadn't promised the bishop anything, but he was too astonished to say a word.

68
00:04:32.928 --> 00:04:36.550
He fled from the bishop's house and the town as fast as he could.

69
00:04:37.051 --> 00:04:39.993
Valjean felt angry, but he wasn't sure with whom.

70
00:04:40.893 --> 00:04:45.376
He didn't know whether he should feel touched—or humiliated—by the bishop's actions.

71
00:04:46.772 --> 00:04:50.134
Perhaps he would be less agitated if the police had taken him to prison.

72
00:04:50.695 --> 00:04:52.536
At least he knew how to deal with prison!

73
00:04:53.296 --> 00:04:58.380
As the sun was setting, Valjean sat by the side of the road only a few miles from

74
00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.140
the bishop's house.

75
00:05:00.021 --> 00:05:04.664
He had been wandering and thinking all day without paying attention to where he was going.

76
00:05:05.645 --> 00:05:09.167
In a few minutes, a young chimney sweep came walking down the road.

77
00:05:09.867 --> 00:05:13.550
The boy was busy singing and tossing a handful of coins in the air.

78
00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.532
He had managed to catch them all on the back of his hand.

79
00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:17.717
Until now.

80
00:05:18.677 --> 00:05:23.720
A silver forty-sou coin got away from him and rolled toward the man sitting by the road.

81
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.562
Valjean promptly put his foot on top of it.

82
00:05:27.382 --> 00:05:30.845
The boy walked over to him and said, "Monsieur, give me my coin."

83
00:05:31.385 --> 00:05:32.085
"What's your name?"

84
00:05:32.105 --> 00:05:33.946
"Little Gervais."

85
00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:37.469
"Go away, Little Gervais," said Valjean, looking at the ground.

86
00:05:38.749 --> 00:05:42.592
The boy repeated his request, and Valjean continued to look at the ground.

87
00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:47.862
Little Gervais tried to move the big, heavy-soled shoe that covered his treasure.

88
00:05:48.282 --> 00:05:51.023
The child began to cry, and Valjean looked up.

89
00:05:51.043 --> 00:05:52.904
"Are you still here?"

90
00:05:53.264 --> 00:05:55.205
Valjean said in a menacing voice.

91
00:05:55.706 --> 00:05:57.866
He stood up suddenly without moving his foot.

92
00:05:58.247 --> 00:06:00.748
"You'd better get going if you know what's good for you."

93
00:06:01.768 --> 00:06:05.150
The boy looked at him in terror before running away as fast as possible.

94
00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:10.092
A few minutes later, Valjean heard him sobbing, and then there was silence.

95
00:06:10.964 --> 00:06:14.347
Valjean continued to sit by the side of the road until it was dark.

96
00:06:14.927 --> 00:06:17.389
When he stood up again, he saw the coin.

97
00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:18.811
"What's this?"

98
00:06:19.191 --> 00:06:22.353
he said to himself, and then he remembered the chimney sweep.

99
00:06:22.814 --> 00:06:23.955
"I've done a bad thing.

100
00:06:24.735 --> 00:06:26.977
I must find that boy and return this to him."

101
00:06:27.838 --> 00:06:32.542
Valjean called the boy's name over and over again, but there was no response.

102
00:06:33.883 --> 00:06:36.645
He started to walk and soon met a priest on horseback.

103
00:06:36.665 --> 00:06:39.868
"Father, have you passed a boy on the road?"

104
00:06:40.208 --> 00:06:40.969
asked Valjean.

105
00:06:40.989 --> 00:06:42.690
"He's about 12 years old."

106
00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.372
"I've seen no one," said the priest.

107
00:06:45.392 --> 00:06:49.135
"Here," said Valjean, handing the priest a few coins.

108
00:06:49.155 --> 00:06:52.338
"Take these and give them to the poor in your parish."

109
00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:56.741
Then he added, "I'm a robber, and you should have me arrested."

110
00:06:57.562 --> 00:06:58.903
The priest fled in fear.

111
00:06:59.423 --> 00:07:02.006
For hours Valjean kept searching for Little Gervais.

112
00:07:02.986 --> 00:07:05.568
Suddenly his knees buckled and he fell to the ground.

113
00:07:06.029 --> 00:07:09.592
It was as if the weight of his guilty conscience had overwhelmed him.

114
00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.782
"What a wretch I am!"

115
00:07:12.062 --> 00:07:16.987
he exclaimed, and he burst into tears for the first time in 19 years.

116
00:07:18.029 --> 00:07:20.151
Valjean realized that he had to change.

117
00:07:20.651 --> 00:07:26.198
When the church clock chimed three on that morning, he was kneeling in prayer at the bishop's door.
